From: Your Name <your.email@example.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 16:41:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] apns: add 3 Sweden IMS and XCAP profiles

Nothing stock ships four profiles for 3/Hallon SE (mcc 240 / mnc 02):
data.tre.se, an ims APN, an xcap APN, and an MMS-over-iWLAN entry. Our
database shipped no ims-type APN for this carrier at all.

An external physical-SIM capture on installed r35 shows the consequence:
across the whole radio log there is not one reference to an ims APN and not
one IMS PDN attempt -- all twelve SETUP_DATA_CALL requests are for
data.tre.se -- while MMTEL repeatedly reports CODE_REGISTRATION_ERROR with
vendor codes 4001 and 4002 on each LTE REG_HOME transition. IMS registration
requires an IMS PDN, which requires an ims-type APN, so it could never
succeed.

Add the ims and xcap rows with stock's exact apn, protocol, roaming_protocol,
and user_visible values, following the ed04060 precedent for AT&T 5G SA.

Deliberately not changed: the "ia" type on the existing data.tre.se row.
Stock sets it, but the initial-attach path was verified working from a
boot-inclusive capture (SET_INITIAL_ATTACH_APN is sent and accepted), so
there is no evidence to justify altering an existing row.

This does not address the separate carrier-independent OEM_DCFAILCAUSE_4
(0x1004) data failure, which remains open.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I65c02baf0ae075246ae6995002cc83bc980b0c18
---
 SE.xml | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/SE.xml b/SE.xml
index 4592524..0459754 100644
--- a/SE.xml
+++ b/SE.xml
@@ -560,6 +560,26 @@
         mmsproxy="mmsproxy.tre.se"
         type="mms"
     />
+    <apn
+        mcc="240"
+        mnc="02"
+        carrier="3 IMS"
+        apn="ims"
+        protocol="IPV4V6"
+        roaming_protocol="IPV4V6"
+        type="ims"
+        user_visible="false"
+    />
+    <apn
+        mcc="240"
+        mnc="02"
+        carrier="3 Ut"
+        apn="services"
+        protocol="IPV4V6"
+        roaming_protocol="IPV4V6"
+        type="xcap"
+        user_visible="false"
+    />
     <apn
         mcc="240"
         mnc="04"
